  "texts": {
    "caption": "Figure 03. Bench-scale continuous-flow photocatalytic oxidation rig. Component tags A1-A13 follow the apparatus list; process steps 1-8 follow the process flow. Connector key: blue solid = material line or process stream, dark grey solid = gas flow, amber dashed = heat, pale yellow dashed = energy, pink dash-dot = control signal, orange solid = recycle loop, pale grey dashed = waste, black solid = split, dark solid = merge. The schematic is not to scale and carries no scale bar.",
    "conclusion": "The rig couples a packed-bed UV-LED reactor to an air-sparged feed and two parallel membrane modules whose retentate is recycled. Conversion rises with catalyst loading up to about 1.2 g/L and then flattens, while the highest rate constant is reached at the shortest residence time."
  },
